cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Si usas este software, cítalo con estos metadatos. If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Cobb coronal en RM lumbar sagital: reproducción abierta y prueba de robustez"
abstract: >-
  Research-only, open and independent reproduction of automated coronal Cobb
  angle measurement on routine sagittal lumbar MRI, using the public SPIDER
  dataset, with a robustness analysis across slice thickness, sequence and
  acquisition site, automatic segmentation and an exploratory endplate-based
  measurement. Since version 0.0.4 it adds two public external datasets
  (RSNA LumbarDISC and the Mendeley Lumbar Spine MRI Dataset), a technical
  review of their automatic segmentations and a preregistered analysis plan
  for the external measurement study. Version 0.0.5 adds that preregistered
  study (T1-T2 agreement, per-face error, noise floor and distribution of the
  angle in both external datasets) and an exploratory follow-up of its
  results. Not a medical device; not for diagnosis.

